 "notes": "Headline limit from Fig. 1: exclusion on g_agamma vs axion mass for hadronic ALPs (gae=0) produced by photon coalescence and trapped in the solar gravitational field, decaying to X-rays. Curve is the envelope of the SphinX coalescence limit (thick dashed blue, ~3.06-6 keV; dash midpoints from the vector EPS in the arXiv e-print) and the stronger NuSTAR coalescence limit (thick blue band, 6-38 keV; midline of the band, whose thickness encodes solar-model uncertainty, max ~1.3x). Axis calibration from ROOT EPS tick positions (x: log, 10 keV at px 1084, 1465 px/decade; y: log, 1e-13 GeV^-1 at px 215, 319.25 px/decade). Limit does not assume ALPs are the local dark matter, so no density rescaling applied (dm_density_assumed null). The paper uses a conservative criterion (predicted ALP-induced flux must not exceed measured solar X-ray flux in each energy bin) and quotes no explicit confidence level; 0.95 entered as placeholder. Masses converted keV -> eV.",
